{"base_rate":0.4953764861294584,"brier":0.19703593130779393,"bss":0.21178887678883063,"bss_hi":0.29900352168006167,"bss_lo":0.12073537819675056,"chart":{"base":[704.3,174.3],"fp":[409.5,285.0],"lead":"62,159.4 272,155.4 482,145.8 692,120.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.21 — higher than 19% of cities","fp":"low end +18pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.0 °C — better than 5% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 22%; promised 93% → rained 81%"},"rel":"78.4,372.3 301.9,284 646.8,118.1"},"country":"GB","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1423778071334214,"ess":387.6209162777405,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Coventry</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Coventry rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>84%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>16%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWELLESBOURNE, 23.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.21, ranked 108 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(72&ndash;118) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>201</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>8%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>94</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>25%</td><td class='num'><b>38%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>84%</b></td><td class='num'>231</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Coventry</b> <span class=\"muted\">GB</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.21</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>72&ndash;118\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Coventry &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Coventry\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text