art-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"201.68295904887714\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"201.68295904887714\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.07432835820895,324.0497512437811 84.70063829787233,258.0851063829787 147.22615384615384,242.0 236.70444444444445,215.7283950617284 330.72749999999996,134.27777777777777 404.0005194805195,74.72727272727275\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 201 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.07432835820895\" cy=\"324.0497512437811\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 8%&amp;#10;It rained 34% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 94 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"84.70063829787233\" cy=\"258.0851063829787\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 25%&amp;#10;It rained 38% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 78 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"147.22615384615384\" cy=\"242.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"236.70444444444445\" cy=\"215.7283950617284\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 77%&amp;#10;It rained 68% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"330.72749999999996\" cy=\"134.27777777777777\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 84% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 231 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"404.0005194805195\" cy=\"74.72727272727275\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(50%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Coventry the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.22) and least in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.05).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'>0.046</td><td class='num'>20.0%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>69%</td><td class='num'>0.090</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.162</td><td class='num'>14.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>0.216</td><td class='num'>13.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":52.40656,"lon":-1.51217,"n":757,"n_cities":134,"name":"Coventry","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.04,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003034825870646766,"n":201,"obs":0.15920398009950248,"sig":true},{"hi":0.16,"lo":0.04,"mean":0.07542553191489361,"n":94,"obs":0.3404255319148936,"sig":true},{